<ttl id="1001O_S001F_74QXD_T00FC" variety="T00FC">
<name>Radar Cruise Control System</name>
<para id="RM00000066500FX" category="J" type-id="803AO" name-id="5915D-00" from="200708">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Vehicle-to-vehicle Distance Switch Circuit</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000066500FX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBQ00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The steering pad switch assembly (distance switch) outputs the distance switching signal to the distance control computer assembly.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Using this signal, the distance control computer assembly sets the vehicle-to-vehicle distance during radar cruise control (vehicle-to-vehicle distance control mode).</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000066500FX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBR00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E143512J03" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000066500FX_07" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBS00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When the distance control computer assembly is replaced with a new one, be sure to perform initialization. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002GO2003X"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000066500FX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000066500FX_08_0017" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBT00000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (C/C Vehicle-to-vehicle Time Setting)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), follow the prompts on the screen to display the "ECU Data Monitor" screen and check the computer data.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor reference values are normal</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[System selection screen: Powertrain → TCCS → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="4" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt> [Item Symbol] </ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Item Description/Display Range</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard Value</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Remarks</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C/C Vehicle-to-vehicle Time Setting</ptxt>
<ptxt> [CDTS] </ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays vehicle setting switch status</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display range = OFF/ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Distance setting switch operated: ON</ptxt>
<ptxt>Distance setting switch not operated: OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Steering Pad SW</ptxt>
<ptxt>Distance control computer</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0023" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0018" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000066500FX_08_0018" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBU00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Steering Pad Switch Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the steering pad switch assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the steering pad switch assembly connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E155195J02" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4(DIST) - 6(ECC)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Distance switch ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4(DIST) - 6(ECC)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Distance switch OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0019" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0024" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000066500FX_08_0019" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBV00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Spiral Cable Sub-assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Center the spiral cable. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000QFE009X_02_0046"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the spiral cable under the following conditions.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E143510J05" width="2.775699831in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>After centering the spiral cable, perform the inspection at the position turned 2.5 turns clockwise and at the position turned 2.5 turns counterclockwise.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Set the spiral cable at the position turned 2.5 turns clockwise from the center position, and measure the resistance while turning it 5.0 turns counterclockwise.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A4(DIST) - C11(DIST)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A6(ECC) - C2(ECC)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.82in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A4 (DIST) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A6 (ECC) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not turn the spiral cable more than the specified number of turns, as this may cause an open circuit.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0020" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000066500FX_08_0025" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000066500FX_08_0020" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CBW00000">
